  },
  "statistic": "median, interquartile range (inclusive quartiles)",
  "warm_up": "one run per arm, excluded; it is also the verification run",
  "wall": "the integration alone, inputs already on the device, to the device synchronised",
  "end_to_end": "inputs uploaded, integration, outputs downloaded",
  "eff_sol": "attempts per second x ops_per_attempt / device_fma_per_s (the register-only DFMA probe run in this script after the arms); ops_per_attempt is the DP-pipe instruction count of one fused eagle attempt (sol_reference.json), audited against cuobjdump in workload.ops_per_attempt_audit",
  "samples_per_lane": "N / (SMs x resident threads per SM)",
  "verification": "Every arm, every sample: final time reached exactly; position error against the analytic Kepler state (Newton on Kepler's equation to machine precision) below the stated bound n_acc tol (1 + v_p)(1 + 6 pi n_orbits v_p), derived from the controller's per-step budget and the Kepler along-track amplification (see truth_bound; not fitted). The truth check runs in the arm's own process; the step counts it returns are compared with the reference arm (eagle graph) in the parent: any difference comes from a floating-point difference flipping one accept/reject decision.",
  "counting_rule": "useful FLOPs = FLOPs per attempt x the attempts the samples actually make (accepted + rejected, summed over samples, as counted by the arm itself); 1106 FLOP per attempt: 1099 counted by running the scheme code (rkf78_stages, kepler_rhs, error_ratio) on a counting number (+, -, x, /, abs, max and sqrt one FLOP each; zero coefficients skipped, as every arm skips them) plus 7 in the controller (the clip, the power, the safety factor, the two-sided clamp, the new step, the new time). The same count for every arm: work a masked arm spends on finished samples, and a batched loop spends past a sample's end, is not useful.",
  "cpu_threads": "8"
 },
